From 9d24050d2507376c6808c31d9811894255d6e79e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:36:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: tell which fidelity step-down levels change
 anything in a render

A caller that lowers the fidelity by itself must not step to a level that
changes nothing: it would spend a window of measurement on it, and keep
times of a level that is not there. Which levels change anything depends
on the renderer and on the frame. Levels 2 and 3 change the upscalers of
the planes of an enhancement layer (libplacebo-9920), and those planes
are drawn only with its residual: libplacebo composes the layer only when
its metadata has NLQ active, and drops it before it draws anything
otherwise (read in renderer.c with the patches of the tree). A renderer
that resampled that layer with filters of its own would leave levels 2
and 3 nothing to change at all.

dvbridge_render_step_levels() gives the levels as a mask, bit n set when
level n draws another picture than the level of the mask above it: 0xf
with the residual of an enhancement layer, 0x3 without it, for every
renderer of this bridge. CDVBridgeGLES::StepLevels() hands it to Kodi.
Nothing that is drawn changes: on the software OpenGL ES, pictures 3, 27
and 51 of the FEL test stream, without a level and at level 0, every
reconstructed picture and every line of hashes and checks of the render
test are byte for byte those of the bridge of rc14-wip with the
libplacebo of before libplacebo-9920, and levels 1 to 3 change the
pictures as they were measured to.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c                     | 8 ++++++++
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h                     | 9 +++++++++
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.h | 6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index 0f88000..3cdf47e 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -661,3 +661,11 @@ int dvbridge_render_step(const struct dvbridge_renderer *r)
 {
     return r ? r->step : 0;
 }
+
+unsigned int dvbridge_render_step_levels(const struct dvbridge_renderer *r, bool residual)
+{
+    /* every renderer of this bridge resamples the planes of an enhancement layer with the
+     * upscalers of step_down() */
+    (void) r;
+    return residual ? 0xfu : 0x3u;
+}
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h
index 5766c9b..571193e 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h
@@ -75,4 +75,13 @@ void dvbridge_render_allow_early_mask(struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer, bool a
 #define DVBRIDGE_STEP_LEVELS 4
 void dvbridge_render_set_step(struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer, int level);
 int dvbridge_render_step(const struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer);
+/* Hades: the step-down levels that change anything in a render of this renderer, as a mask: bit n is
+ * set when level n draws another picture than the level of the mask above it (bit 0, the faithful
+ * picture, always is). residual: the render draws the residual of an enhancement layer. With it,
+ * levels 1, 2 and 3 all do: this renderer has the planes of that layer scaled up with the upscalers
+ * that levels 2 and 3 change (libplacebo-9920). Without it no plane of that layer is drawn (there is
+ * none, or libplacebo leaves out a layer whose metadata reconstructs no residual), and only level 1
+ * does. A caller that lowers the fidelity by itself steps only between the levels of the mask: a
+ * level outside it would change nothing. */
+unsigned int dvbridge_render_step_levels(const struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer, bool residual);
 #endif
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.h
index 2f2995c..c4c247a 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.h
@@ -53,6 +53,12 @@ public:
   //! dvbridge_render_set_step()). 0, the faithful picture, until it is set; Reset() keeps it
   void SetStepLevel(int level) { dvbridge_render_set_step(m_renderer, level); }
   int StepLevel() const { return dvbridge_render_step(m_renderer); }
+  //! Hades: the step-down levels that change anything in a frame prepared with, or without, the
+  //! residual of an enhancement layer (see dvbridge_render_step_levels())
+  unsigned int StepLevels(bool residual) const
+  {
+    return dvbridge_render_step_levels(m_renderer, residual);
+  }
   /*!
    * \brief What the work of preparing a frame depends on, from its metadata, before it is prepared
    * \param enhancement the frame comes with a picture of its enhancement layer
-- 
2.53.0

